Question Title: Advanced File Management

Question Link: https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/4ks5o139cfoh?lecture_hash=v210chxjexei

Solution:
mkdir project-files
cd project-files
touch report.docx summary.docx draft.docx
cp report.docx report_backup.docx
mkdir old
mv draft.docx old
mv summary.docx final_summary.docx
cp final_summary.docx old
rm report_backup.docx

Approach:
1. Created a folder called project-files.
2. Created three empty files: report.docx, summary.docx, draft.docx.
3. Copied report.docx to report_backup.docx to make a backup.
4. Created a folder called oldx.
5. Moved draft.docx into old.
6. Renamed summary.docx to final_summary.docx using mv.
7. Copied final_summary.docx into old.
8. Deleted report_backup.docx since it was no longer needed.